{
 "section_summary": "This section contains translated transcripts of Japanese shortwave broadcasts, chiefly Station JLU4 programs dated August 1–10, 1941, preceded by the end of an earlier transcript and an FBI cover letter. The broadcasts report Japan’s deployment in French Indochina, trade restrictions and asset freezes, pressure on Thailand, fighting in China, and the German invasion of the Soviet Union. Their commentaries promote the Greater East Asia Mutual Prosperity Sphere and portray British and American actions as hostile to Japan.",
